From 07d8fdcb6dd31ec6f5bef538f7d80683f63aa1a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:56:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/43] test: the help golden lists the checked-exceptions
 option and its warning group

Expected consequence of adding an option (gap-analysis C14): '--enable-chexc' with its two
severities, and 'chexc' in both the -Woff and -Won group lists. The suite is green again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 testsuites/LLT/compiler/Driver/options/help/test_showall.cj | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/testsuites/LLT/compiler/Driver/options/help/test_showall.cj b/testsuites/LLT/compiler/Driver/options/help/test_showall.cj
index 3556a8f150..994b23d727 100644
--- a/testsuites/LLT/compiler/Driver/options/help/test_showall.cj
+++ b/testsuites/LLT/compiler/Driver/options/help/test_showall.cj
@@ -54,6 +54,10 @@ Options:
   --profile-compile-time      Write time spent of all phases to <package>.time.prof in the output directory
   --profile-compile-memory    Write memory usage of all phases to <package>.mem.prof in the output directory
   --enable-eh                 Enables experimental support for effect handlers (Experimental)
+  --enable-chexc, --enable-checked-exceptions
+                              Enables experimental support for checked exceptions. Candidate severities: (Experimental)
+    <value>=error               report capability violations as errors (default)
+    <value>=warn                report capability violations as warnings
   --dump-ast                  Dump human readable AST when compiling for debug
   --dump-chir                 Dump human readable CHIR when compiling for debug
   --dump-ir                   Dump human readable IR
@@ -138,6 +142,7 @@ Options:
     <value>=semantics           
     <value>=interpreter         
     <value>=apilevel-check      
+    <value>=chexc               
   -Won, --warn-on <value>     Report a specific group of warning
     <value>=all                 
     <value>=unused              
@@ -150,6 +155,7 @@ Options:
     <value>=semantics           
     <value>=interpreter         
     <value>=apilevel-check      
+    <value>=chexc               
   --error-count-limit <value> Emit specified <number> of errors only. Available options: all, <number> (8 by default)
   -V, --verbose               Enable verbose
   -v, --version               Print compiler version information 
